Dockerfile

# Real secrets (VITE_ARCGIS_API_KEY, VITE_ARCGIS_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID) live here.
# Without this, `COPY my-arcgis-app/. .` in the Dockerfile's build stage
# copies my-arcgis-app/.env straight into that stage's image layer - even
# though the final nginx stage only copies dist/ out of it, the build
# stage's own layers (and anything built with --target build, or pushed/
# cached) still contain the raw file. Build-time config must reach the
# image only via explicit ARG/ENV (see Dockerfile), never via a copied
# .env - Compose already reads .env directly off disk to fill in those
# ARGs' values without it ever entering the build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example